  "about": "Only what her host says is granted on this link decides, never what it said on a link before. A call that comes before it has said (her host sending again, on a new link, an ask that went into one already gone) waits: it is acked, not handed to the shell and not answered. When her host says what is granted here, each waiting call is judged by that: handed to the shell, or answered call_not_granted, which is what becomes of a call for an action the owner took back while the link was down. One that waits is still held to its deadline and can be cancelled, and no one is told to stop, since the shell never had it. One that waits when the link goes waits for the next link's word.",
